Algorithm:
1.Start the program.
2.Define a node structure containing data, height, left pointer, and right pointer.
3.Initialize the AVL tree with a NULL root.
4.Accept the number of elements from the user.
5.Read the elements one by one.
6.Insert each element according to Binary Search Tree insertion rules.
7.Update the height of each node after insertion.
8.Calculate the balance factor using:
Balance Factor = Height of Left Subtree − Height of Right Subtree
9.Check whether the balance factor indicates an LL imbalance.
10.If an LL imbalance is detected:
Display the unbalanced subtree.
Display the balance factors of the affected nodes.
Perform a right rotation.
Display the balanced subtree and updated balance factors.
11.Handle other imbalance cases (RR, LR, and RL) using their respective rotations.
12.Display the final AVL tree.
13.Display the inorder traversal of the tree.
14.Report whether an LL imbalance was detected.
15.Stop the program.
